Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- core/stats/curve_designs.py:
  - curve_in_blocks — polynomial (centred powers) or transformed-x curve
    with the block fitted first (intra-block analysis, 15.3) and the
    lack-of-fit factor of x levels (12.8): sequential ANOVA with
    Group and powers.Group terms, automatic choice of common, parallel or
    separate curves, parameters, predictions and curves for an average
    block with CIs.
  - nonlinear_in_blocks — exponential, inverse linear, logistic,
    Gompertz or power curve with block shifts of the level α and nested
    group models (common → separate α → separate α, β → all separate,
    p. 476) compared by F against the most general model; lack of fit
    against Block + FacX; fitting by variable projection (θ by
    Levenberg–Marquardt, linear parameters by least squares), SEs from
    the full Jacobian, delta-method bands.
- Tests: degree 1 reproduces Table 15.13 and blocked_regression;
  quadratic sums of squares and averaged-block prediction SE equal
  statsmodels OLS; no-block nonlinear fit reproduces Example 17.1C;
  blocked exponential estimates and SEs equal scipy curve_fit with
  explicit block indicators; group-model sequence on simulated data.

